  - latent reasoning
  - retrieval
  - matched controls
  - process of elimination
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >
  Synthesis is the adversarial case for a transport account of LLM behaviour: in an
  A->B->C->D chain the answer D is absent and must be assembled. Pre-registered and
  cross-model (Llama-3.2-3B, Qwen2.5-3B), implicit multi-hop reasoning reduces to
  retrieval-and-elimination: corrupting the middle hop flips correct answers in only
  5-11% of cases while corrupting the code fact flips 100%, masking link facts at the
  answer step is inert, and blocking elimination with decoys floors accuracy to
  chance. Explicit chain-of-thought traverses genuinely (a positive control: 84-90%
  middle-hop flip) but only by writing each hop into context and re-reading it
  (self-delivery), not by internal decode-time binding. A methodological catch: node
  removal is confounded by elimination under competition; in-place corruption is the
  faithful usage test. At 3B, internal multi-hop computation of an absent fact does
  not occur; composition appears only as externalized self-delivery.
